<title>SWITZERLAND: FIGURE SKATING-URMANOV WITHDRAWS FROM WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS.</title>
<headline>FIGURE SKATING-URMANOV WITHDRAWS FROM WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS.</headline>
<dateline>LAUSANNE, Switzerland 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Olympic champion Alexei Urmanov withdrew from the world championships on Thursday night with a leg injury.</p>
<p>The 23-year-old European champion, bidding for his first world title, pulled a groin muscle during the short programme on Wednesday and, after the final warmup for the free programme, he decided to withdraw.</p>
